                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s34IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُم أَيُّهَا المُرْسَلُونَ , قَالُوا إنَّا أُرْسِلْنَا إلَى قَوم مُجْرِمِينَ</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#11r">-11r</locus>أَلَّا يَقْدِرُونَ عَلَى شَئٍ مِن فَضْلِ الله وَ[.؟.]دِ اللهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَن يَشَأُ وَاللهُ ذُو الفَضْـ<note>Part of the folio torn.</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>51:31-57:29. Penciled pagination. Titles of suras rubricated in red. Three dots as verse markers. Red double frames. FIne qalam. Professional hand. Ihmāl marks (kāf-s). When the last letter of the last word of a line does not reach the red frame leaving an empty space, the copyist used a sign to fill out the line (ex. 1v, 3v, 4v, 5v, etc.). Saǧda mark in red in the margin of fol. 4v.</note>
                     <note/>
